 ## 5\. Core Features

 ### A. Smart Expense Tracker

 Users can enter expenses manually:

```
Food       ₹250
Transport  ₹80
Shopping   ₹1,200
Bills      ₹2,000
```

 AI automatically categorizes expenses.

 Possible categories:

 - Food
- Transport
- Housing
- Utilities
- Shopping
- Entertainment
- Education
- Healthcare
- Subscriptions
- Other

---

 ### B. AI Budget Generator

 Instead of requiring users to manually calculate everything, PocketSmart can generate a starting budget from:

 - Monthly income
- Fixed expenses
- Variable expenses
- Savings goal
- Debt payments
- Financial priorities

 Example:

```
Monthly Income: ₹30,000

Needs             ₹16,000
Wants              ₹6,000
Savings            ₹5,000
Emergency Fund     ₹3,000
```

 The user can then modify the suggested amounts.

---

 ### C. AI Spending Insights

 The assistant identifies patterns such as:

 > “Your food spending increased 18% compared with last month.”

 > “You spent ₹1,450 on subscriptions this month.”

 > “Weekend spending represents 42% of your entertainment expenses.”

 This turns raw transaction data into understandable information.

---

 ### D. Smart Recommendations

 Recommendations can include:

 - Reduce a particular spending category
- Set a spending limit
- Review unused subscriptions
- Increase emergency savings
- Adjust a budget category
- Set a short-term savings goal

 Recommendations should be **explainable and user-controlled**, rather than automatically making financial decisions.

---

 ### E. “Can I Afford It?” Assistant

 A conversational feature where users ask:

 > “Can I buy a ₹5,000 smartwatch?”

 > “Can I afford a weekend trip?”

 > “Should I spend ₹1,500 on this game?”

 The AI considers the user's configured budget and upcoming obligations and explains the financial impact.

---

 ### F. Savings Goal Planner

 Users can create goals:

```
Goal: New Laptop
Target: ₹60,000
Current Savings: ₹15,000
Deadline: 8 months
```

 PocketSmart calculates a required monthly contribution and tracks progress.

